sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Write the system default for OpenGL stereo from the graphics card the
    desktop runs on, at install, at boot and when a card is added, removed
    or changes driver. When NVIDIA's driver runs the desktop, the session's
    programs run their OpenGL on Mesa over NVIDIA's Vulkan driver (zink),
    where a program that draws its own two views gets them, started from
    the menu, the panel or a terminal; KWin and Xwayland keep NVIDIA's
    driver. A desktop on Mesa keeps Mesa. sparky-stereo-opengl-default
    --opengl nvidia keeps NVIDIA's own OpenGL instead.
  * Complete this changelog with versions 0.1.7 and 0.1.8.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300

sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Live sessions choose the NVIDIA driver at boot: the edition's open
    modules for Turing and newer, nouveau for older, mixed or unknown
    cards, for a kernel without the modules and for unsigned modules under
    Secure Boot; sparky.gpu=nvidia or sparky.gpu=nouveau overrides it.
  * A notification says which driver runs the NVIDIA graphics in a live
    session, and why.
  * KWin renders on a card that can render, with a screen connected, when
    the boot VGA device is a BMC's VGA chip.
  * German, Japanese, Korean and Chinese (simplified and traditional)
    strings.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0300

